# Chat reply

Import WireNumber from "./wire_number.lg".
Import WireRead from "./wire_read.lg".
Import WireShape from "./wire_shape.lg".

What a model answered, read: the first choice's text and finish reason, the
reported token counts, and the reported cost in dollars rounded up to a
micro-dollar. An OpenRouter error document is an error, with its code.

## Note
`costMicros` is OpenRouter's own reported cost when the reply carries one;
`usageKnown` says whether the reply reported its token counts at all.

## A ChatReply has:
    an id, which is Text.
    a model, which is Text.
    a content, which is Text.
    a finishReason, which is Text.
    a usageKnown, which is Bool.
    a promptTokens, which is Int.
    a completionTokens, which is Int.
    a costMicros, which is Option of Int.

## Note
The message of an error document, or the empty text.

## To errorOfReply (v: Json) -> Text:
    If jsonHas(v, "error") is equal to false:
        Return "".
    Let e be jsonGet(v, "error").
    Inspect jsonGet(e, "code"):
        When JNum (code):
            Return "OpenRouter error {code}: " + textAt(e, "message").
        Otherwise:
            Return "OpenRouter error: " + textAt(e, "message").
    Return "OpenRouter error".

## Note
The first choice's content and finish reason, or why there is none.

## To firstChoice (v: Json) -> Result of (Text, Text) and Text:
    Inspect jsonGet(v, "choices"):
        When JArr (choices):
            If length of choices is equal to 0:
                Return a new Err with error "the reply has no choices".
            Let first be item 1 of choices.
            Inspect jsonGet(jsonGet(first, "message"), "content"):
                When JStr (s):
                    Return a new Ok with value (s, textAt(first, "finish_reason")).
                Otherwise:
                    Return a new Err with error "the first choice has no text content".
        Otherwise:
            Return a new Err with error "the reply has no choices".
    Return a new Err with error "the reply has no choices".

## Note
A reply's text, read.

## To parseChatReply (text: Text) -> Result of ChatReply and Text:
    Inspect parseStrict(text):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error "the reply is not JSON: " + e.
        When Ok (v):
            If errorOfReply(v) is not equal to "":
                Return a new Err with error errorOfReply(v).
            Inspect firstChoice(v):
                When Err (e):
                    Return a new Err with error e.
                When Ok (choice):
                    Let (content, finish) be choice.
                    Let usage be jsonGet(v, "usage").
                    Let mutable reply be a new ChatReply with id textAt(v, "id") and model textAt(v, "model") and content content and finishReason finish.
                    Set reply's usageKnown to openShapeProblem(usage, ["prompt_tokens:int", "completion_tokens:int"]) is equal to "".
                    Set reply's promptTokens to intAt(usage, "prompt_tokens").
                    Set reply's completionTokens to intAt(usage, "completion_tokens").
                    Set reply's costMicros to none.
                    If jsonHas(usage, "cost"):
                        Inspect jsonScaledCeil(jsonGet(usage, "cost"), 6):
                            When Ok (micros):
                                Set reply's costMicros to some micros.
                            When Err (e):
                                Return a new Err with error "the reply's cost is unreadable: " + e.
                    Return a new Ok with value reply.
    Return a new Err with error "unreadable reply".
